{"depth":"full","paper_type":"observational_alma_primary","paper_type_evidence":[{"loc":"Introduction","quote":"In this paper we present new observations of 9io9 with the Atacama Large Millimeter/sub-millimeter Array (ALMA), building on the work of (cite: geach_magnified_2018)."}],"fields":["high_z_galaxies"],"question":{"value":"What is the average electron density of the ionised ISM in the lensed SMG 9io9 at z=2.6, from the [N II] 122/205 micron line ratio, and how does it relate to the dense molecular gas?","evidence":[{"loc":"abstract","quote":"The 122-/205-$\mu$m [N ii] line ratio is sensitive to electron density, $n_{\rm e}$, in the ionised interstellar medium, and we use this to measure $n_{\rm e}\approx 300\,\text{cm}^{-3}$ averaged across the galaxy."}]},"targets":[{"name":"9io9","details":[{"loc":"Observations","quote":"9io9 ($02^{\rm h}09^{\rm m}41.3s$, $00\ensuremath{^\circ}15\ensuremath{'}58.5\ensuremath{''}$, $z=2.5543$)"},{"loc":"Introduction","quote":"Even after taking into account the 15$\times$ magnification factor"}],"coordinates":"02h09m41.3s, +00d15m58.5s","redshift_or_distance":"z = 2.5543; magnification about 15x","distance_source":"not stated"}],"alma_project_codes":[{"code":"2017.1.00814.S","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations","quote":"was observed with the ALMA 12-m array in project 2017.1.00814.S in Bands 4, 8 and 9."}]}],"data_settings":[{"field":"bands","value":"Bands 4, 8, 9 (new data: Bands 8 and 9)","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations","quote":"The details of the Band 4 observations are presented in (cite: geach_magnified_2018), and here we present the new Band 8 and 9 data."}]},{"field":"frequencies_and_spectral_setup","value":"Band 8: four SPWs at 397.466, 399.404, 409.481, 411.481 GHz; Band 9: eight SPWs from 670.311 to 692.138 GHz","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations","quote":"The central frequencies of the four spectral windows were 397.466, 399.404, 409.481 and 411.481 GHz"},{"loc":"Observations","quote":"eight spectral windows at 670.311, 672.249, 674.249, 676.202, 686.248, 688.201, 690.200 and 692.138 GHz"}]},{"field":"arrays","value":"ALMA 12-m array","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations","quote":"was observed with the ALMA 12-m array in project 2017.1.00814.S in Bands 4, 8 and 9."}]},{"field":"configurations","value":"Band 8: C43-4 (47 antennas); Band 9: C43-3 (46 antennas)","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations","quote":"The antenna configuration was C43–4 (with 47 antennas), with a maximum baseline of 783 m."},{"loc":"Observations","quote":"The antenna configuration was C43–3 (with 46 antennas), with a maximum baseline of 484 m."}]},{"field":"baselines","value":"Max baseline 783 m (Band 8), 484 m (Band 9)","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations","quote":"with a maximum baseline of 484 m"}]},{"field":"angular_resolution","value":"Natural weighting beams 0.43x0.35 arcsec (Band 8), 0.32x0.28 arcsec (Band 9); tapered to 0.6 arcsec","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations","quote":"With natural weighting, the synthesised beams were $0.43\ensuremath{''} \times 0.35\ensuremath{''}$ (FWHM, position angle $33\ensuremath{^\circ}$)"}]},{"field":"max_recoverable_scale","value":"LAS <~ 3-4 arcsec","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations","quote":"(LAS $\lesssim$3–4$''$)"}]},{"field":"sensitivity","value":"Band 8: 3 mJy/beam per 15.6-MHz channel; Band 9: 10 mJy/beam per 15.6-MHz channel","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations","quote":"resulting in an r.m.s. noise of 3 mJy beam$^{-1}$ in a 15.6-MHz channel"},{"loc":"Observations","quote":"resulting in an r.m.s. noise of 10 mJy beam$^{-1}$ in a 15.6-MHz channel"}]},{"field":"time_on_source","value":"Band 8: 42 min; Band 9: 31 min","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations","quote":"the total on-source integration time was 42 min"},{"loc":"Observations","quote":"The total time on-source was 31 min"}]},{"field":"observing_dates","value":"Band 8: 2018 Aug 26 and Sep 07; Band 9: 2018 Aug 19","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations","quote":"The Band 8 observations were conducted on 2018 August 26 and 2018 September 07"},{"loc":"Observations","quote":"The Band 9 observations were conducted on 2018 August 19 in a single 70-min execution block."}]}],"lines_targeted":[{"species":"[N II]","transition":"3P1-3P0 (205 um)","rest_frequency":"1461.131 GHz","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations","quote":"$^{3}P_{1}$$\rightarrow$$^{3}P_{0}$ fine-structure line ($\nu_{\text{rest}} = 1461.131$ GHz)"}]},{"species":"[N II]","transition":"3P2-3P1 (122 um)","rest_frequency":"2459.380 GHz","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations","quote":"$^{3}P_{2}$$\rightarrow$$^{3}P_{1}$ fine-structure line ($\nu_{\text{rest}} = 2459.380$ GHz)"}]}],"other_facilities":[],"external_data_from_literature":[{"what":{"value":"Band 4 ALMA data with CO(4-3) and CI(1-0) lines and the lens model of 9io9","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations","quote":"The details of the Band 4 observations are presented in (cite: geach_magnified_2018)"}]},"citation":"(cite: geach_magnified_2018)"},{"what":{"value":"N+ collision rate coefficients at Te = 8000 K","evidence":[{"loc":"Electron density","quote":"Using collision rates from (cite: tayal_electron_2011) for a kinetic temperature, $T_{\text e} = 8000$ K"}]},"citation":"(cite: tayal_electron_2011)"}],"simulations_or_models_as_data":[],"calibration":[{"field":"pipeline_or_manual","value":"Band 8: pipeline-restored calibrated MS; Band 9: manual re-calibration, flagging antennas DA64 and DA24","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations","quote":"For the Band 8 data we used the pipeline-restored calibrated measurement set."},{"loc":"Observations","quote":"due to unstable phases in two antennas (DA64 and DA24) we re-calibrated manually"}]},{"field":"archive_products_used_as_is","value":"Band 8 pipeline-restored calibrated measurement set used","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations","quote":"For the Band 8 data we used the pipeline-restored calibrated measurement set."}]}],"imaging":[{"field":"task","value":"CASA tclean (v.5.1.0-74.el7)","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations","quote":"We imaged and cleaned the data using the casa (v.5.1.0-74.el7) task, `tclean`."}]},{"field":"deconvolver","value":"multi-scale clean at scales 0, 0.5, 1.25 arcsec","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations","quote":"we employ multi-scale cleaning (at scales of $0\ensuremath{''}, 0.5\ensuremath{''},$and$, 1.25\ensuremath{''}$)"}]},{"field":"weighting_robust","value":"natural weighting","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations","quote":"With natural weighting, the synthesised beams were"}]},{"field":"uv_taper","value":"0.6 arcsec","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations","quote":"we also produce *uv*-tapered maps with a scale of 0.6$''$"}]},{"field":"masking","value":"dirty cubes to set per-channel rms, then clean to 3 sigma threshold","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations","quote":"First we produce dirty cubes to establish the r.m.s. (1$\sigma$) noise per channel, and then clean down to a threshold of 3$\sigma$."}]},{"field":"continuum_subtraction","value":"per-pixel linear fit (free gradient and normalisation) to line-free regions of the cube","evidence":[{"loc":"Line and continuum measurements","quote":"Subtracting the continuum model from each pixel based on a linear fit to line free regions of the lines corresponding data cube allowing the gradient and normalisation vary as free parameters"}]},{"field":"final_beam","value":"0.43x0.35 arcsec (Band 8), 0.32x0.28 arcsec (Band 9) natural; source-plane average beam 280 mas (2.3 kpc)","evidence":[{"loc":"Lens model","quote":"The resulting source plane reconstruction has an average beam size of $280\,\text{mas}$ (FWHM) corresponding to a physical scale of 2.3 kpc in the source plane."}]}],"inherited":[{"what":{"value":"Multi-scale cleaning approach","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations","quote":"As in (cite: geach_magnified_2018), we employ multi-scale cleaning"}]},"from_reference":"(cite: geach_magnified_2018)"},{"what":{"value":"Lens model (two-galaxy potential, semi-linear inversion)","evidence":[{"loc":"Lens model","quote":"We adopt the same lens model as (cite: geach_magnified_2018)."}]},"from_reference":"(cite: geach_magnified_2018)"},{"what":{"value":"Rate-equation formalism for [N II] levels","evidence":[{"loc":"Electron density","quote":"Following (cite: goldsmith_herschel_2015), the rate equations can be written"}]},"from_reference":"(cite: goldsmith_herschel_2015)"}],"unstated_but_needed":["Lens model parameters and the source-plane reconstruction code/setup (in Geach et al. 2018)","Cell size, image size, channel width and velocity resolution of the cubes","Line-free channel ranges used for continuum fitting","Modified blackbody details: beta/Td fit results, fit method, rest-frame wavelengths and flux errors","Flux calibrator and flux scale uncertainty","Band 9 manual calibration details","Source-plane mask construction and how the 3 sigma region was defined for the ratio","How the n_e uncertainty was propagated from the flux errors","Data and sources used for Fig. 4 literature comparison"],"analysis_steps":[{"order":1,"goal":"Calibrate and image Band 8/9 cubes","method":{"value":"Pipeline-restored data (Band 8) or manual recalibration (Band 9), tclean multiscale, natural weighting, plus 0.6 arcsec taper","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations","quote":"We imaged and cleaned the data using the casa (v.5.1.0-74.el7) task, `tclean`."}]},"software":["CASA"],"key_parameters":[{"value":"clean to 3 sigma; scales 0, 0.5, 1.25 arcsec","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations","quote":"then clean down to a threshold of 3$\sigma$"}]}],"assumptions":[],"fitting":{"value":"not stated","evidence":[]},"validation":{"value":"uv plane well sampled, negligible extended-emission losses expected","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations","quote":"we expect negligible losses to extended emission on the scale of the lens"}]}},{"order":2,"goal":"Reconstruct source-plane cubes","method":{"value":"Semi-linear inversion with the Geach et al. 2018 lens model; each slice reconstructed with 50 randomised Voronoi grids, averaged weighted by log-likelihood","evidence":[{"loc":"Lens model","quote":"Each slice was reconstructed with 50 realisations of a randomised Voronoi source plane grid (cite: dye_modelling_2018) and the mean taken, weighted by the log of the likelihood of each realisation."}]},"software":[],"key_parameters":[{"value":"50 Voronoi realisations per slice","evidence":[{"loc":"Lens model","quote":"Each slice was reconstructed with 50 realisations of a randomised Voronoi source plane grid"}]}],"assumptions":[{"value":"Errors exclude systematic uncertainty of the parametric lens model","evidence":[{"loc":"Lens model","quote":"The errors quoted for the intrinsic source properties do not include any systematic uncertainty introduced by the prescribed parametric lens model"}]}],"fitting":{"value":"not stated","evidence":[]},"validation":{"value":"not stated","evidence":[]}},{"order":3,"goal":"Measure L_IR from continuum SED","method":{"value":"Single-temperature modified blackbody fit with free beta, Td, normalisation; luminosity summed within the 3 sigma Band 8 contour in the source plane","evidence":[{"loc":"Line and continuum measurements","quote":"We fit the observed emission with a single-temperature modified blackbody spectrum, allowing the dust emissivity ($\beta$), dust temperature ($T_{\rm d}$) and normalisation to be free parameters."}]},"software":[],"key_parameters":[{"value":"L_IR defined at rest-frame 8-1000 um","evidence":[{"loc":"Line and continuum measurements","quote":"we can estimate $L_{\rm IR}$ (rest-frame 8–1000 $\mu$m)"}]}],"assumptions":[],"fitting":{"value":"not stated","evidence":[]},"validation":{"value":"not stated","evidence":[]}},{"order":4,"goal":"Measure [N II] line fluxes and luminosities","method":{"value":"Subtract linear continuum per pixel, integrate within the 3 sigma mask, convert with the Solomon et al. 1997 relation; Monte Carlo errors by adding Gaussian noise (1000 realisations)","evidence":[{"loc":"Line and continuum measurements","quote":"Repeating this 1000 times and integrating the lines for each realisation allows us to estimate the uncertainties."}]},"software":[],"key_parameters":[{"value":"122 um integrated over -500 to 300 km/s because lines are incomplete","evidence":[{"loc":"Line and continuum measurements","quote":"integrating between $-500~\text{km}~\text{s}^{-1}$ and $300~\text{km}~\text{s}^{-1}$ due to the [N ii] lines being incomplete"}]}],"assumptions":[{"value":"About 10% of line flux missed for both lines, so the ratio is unaffected","evidence":[{"loc":"Line and continuum measurements","quote":"we estimate we are missing $\approx 10\%$ of the total line flux for both lines"}]},{"value":"Planck 2015 cosmology, H0=68, Omega_m=0.31","evidence":[{"loc":"Introduction","quote":"$H_{0} = 68~\text{km}~\text{s}^{-1}\,\text{Mpc}^{-1}$ and $\Omega_{\text{m}} = 0.31$"}]}],"fitting":{"value":"not stated","evidence":[]},"validation":{"value":"not stated","evidence":[]}},{"order":5,"goal":"Derive electron density from the line ratio","method":{"value":"Three-level N+ rate equations with electron collisions, Tayal collision rates at Te=8000 K, giving n_e = 247 (R-0.52)/(9.73-R) cm^-3","evidence":[{"loc":"Electron density","quote":"$$\begin{equation}
 \label{eq:ne247}
    n_{\text{e}}=247\left(\frac{R - 0.52}{9.73-R}\right)\text{cm}^{-3}.
\end{equation}$$"}]},"software":[],"key_parameters":[{"value":"Te = 8000 K; collision rates assumed temperature independent","evidence":[{"loc":"Electron density","quote":"assuming that collision rates are independent of temperature"}]}],"assumptions":[{"value":"Optically thin emission; column density ratio equals volume density ratio","evidence":[{"loc":"Electron density","quote":"assuming the ratio of column densities equals the ratio of volume densities"}]}],"fitting":{"value":"not stated","evidence":[]},"validation":{"value":"n_e changes by under 10% for a 2000 K increase in temperature; optical pumping tested at about 2% of collision rate","evidence":[{"loc":"Electron density","quote":"the derived electron density does not vary by more than 10% for a 2000 K increase in kinetic temperature"},{"loc":"Electron density","quote":"or approximately 2 per cent of the collision rate"}]}}],"software":[{"name":"CASA","version":"v.5.1.0-74.el7","used_for":{"value":"Imaging and cleaning with tclean","evidence":[{"loc":"Observations","quote":"We imaged and cleaned the data using the casa (v.5.1.0-74.el7) task, `tclean`."}]}}],"results_numeric":[{"quantity":"L_IR (8-1000 um)","value":"1.1e13","uncertainty":"0.2e13","units":"Lsun","from_step":3,"evidence":[{"loc":"Line and continuum measurements","quote":"we measure a total $L_{\rm IR}=(1.1\pm 0.2)\times 10^{13}\,\mathrm{L}_\odot$"}]},{"quantity":"[N II] 205um integrated flux","value":"2.37","uncertainty":"0.06","units":"Jy km/s","from_step":4,"evidence":[{"loc":"Line and continuum measurements","quote":"$\mathbf{S}\Delta V = (2.37 \pm 0.06)~\text{Jy~km}~\text{s}^{-1}$"}]},{"quantity":"L_205","value":"4.7e8","uncertainty":"0.1e8","units":"Lsun","from_step":4,"evidence":[{"loc":"Line and continuum measurements","quote":"$L_{205}=(4.7 \pm 0.1) \times 10^{8} \,\mathrm{L}_\odot$"}]},{"quantity":"[N II] 122um integrated flux","value":"7.6","uncertainty":"0.9","units":"Jy km/s","from_step":4,"evidence":[{"loc":"Line and continuum measurements","quote":"the integrated flux density is S$\Delta V = (7.6 \pm 0.9)~\text{Jy~km}~\text{s}^{-1}$"}]},{"quantity":"L_122","value":"2.6e9","uncertainty":"0.3e9","units":"Lsun","from_step":4,"evidence":[{"loc":"Line and continuum measurements","quote":"$L_{122}=(2.6 \pm 0.3) \times 10^{9} \,\mathrm{L}_\odot$"}]},{"quantity":"Electron density","value":"290","uncertainty":"+90/-70","units":"cm^-3","from_step":5,"evidence":[{"loc":"Electron density","quote":"we find an electron density of $n_{\text{e}} = 290^{+90}_{-70}\text{cm}^{-3}$"}]},{"quantity":"Source-plane continuum flux density at 400 and 680 GHz","value":"12 mJy and 43 mJy","uncertainty":"not stated","units":"mJy","from_step":3,"evidence":[{"loc":"Line and continuum measurements","quote":"the total Band 8 and Band 9 source plane continuum flux densities are 12 mJy and 43 mJy at observed frequencies of 400 and 680 GHz"}]}],"findings_qualitative":[{"value":"[N II] line profiles resemble the CO(4-3) and CI(1-0) profiles, so ionised and molecular gas are co-located","evidence":[{"loc":"Interpretation and discussion","quote":"indicating that the ionised and molecular tracers originate from the same material and local environments"}]},{"value":"Weak trend of higher [N II] ratio with higher CO(4-3)/CI(1-0) ratio across literature sources","evidence":[{"loc":"Interpretation and discussion","quote":"there is a weak trend that galaxies or regions with high electron densities"}]}],"claims":[{"hypothesis":"Is the ionised ISM of 9io9 dense on global scales?","experiment":"Measured [N II] 122/205 um ratio in the source plane and converted to n_e","result":"n_e = 290 (+90/-70) cm^-3","finding":"Globally averaged n_e is over an order of magnitude above the Milky Way average, comparable to Galactic star-forming regions","support":"supported","evidence":[{"loc":"abstract","quote":"This is over an order of magnitude higher than the Milky Way average, but comparable to localised Galactic star-forming regions."}]},{"hypothesis":"Is the ionised gas co-located with the molecular gas?","experiment":"Compared [N II] line profiles with CO(4-3) and CI(1-0)","result":"Double-horned profiles match","finding":"Ionised gas broadly co-located with molecular material on kpc scales","support":"supported","evidence":[{"loc":"Conclusions","quote":"This implies that the ionised gas is broadly co-located with the molecular material on scales of several kiloparsecs."}]},{"hypothesis":"Does the ionised gas density track the dense molecular gas fraction?","experiment":"Compared [N II] ratio with CO(4-3)/CI(1-0) for 9io9 and literature sources","result":"Tentative trend","finding":"Picture of a globally dense ISM","support":"partially","evidence":[{"loc":"Conclusions","quote":"We demonstrate a tentative (but expected) trend between the ratio of dense molecular gas and the total molecular gas reservoir"}]}],"reasoning":[{"field":"why_this_data","value":"Lensing amplification allows [N II] diagnostics that would be impossible for unlensed targets","evidence":[{"loc":"Introduction","quote":"their lens-amplified flux offers a route to measure diagnostic tracers of the ISM and its conditions in a way that would be impossible in the unlensed case"}]}],"alternatives_considered_or_rejected":[{"value":"Resolved 122 um properties and resolved line ratio not interpreted due to low S/N","evidence":[{"loc":"Lens model","quote":"we do not attempt to interpret the resolved properties of the line itself, or the line ratio, concentrating our analysis on the integrated properties"}]}],"limitations_admitted":[{"value":"Errors exclude lens-model systematics","evidence":[{"loc":"Lens model","quote":"The errors quoted for the intrinsic source properties do not include any systematic uncertainty introduced by the prescribed parametric lens model"}]},{"value":"Lines incomplete in the band coverage; roughly 10% flux missing","evidence":[{"loc":"Line and continuum measurements","quote":"we estimate we are missing $\approx 10\%$ of the total line flux for both lines"}]}],"referee_caveats_inferred":["Single-temperature, temperature-independent collision-rate assumption for n_e","Low S/N of the 122 um line","Trend with CO/CI ratio rests on a heterogeneous literature sample","Lens model inherited without independent check"],"reproducibility":[{"field":"data_public_as_stated","value":"ALMA data acknowledged by project code; public status not stated","evidence":[{"loc":"Acknowledgements","quote":"This paper makes use of the following ALMA data: ADS/JAO.ALMA#2017.1.00814.S."}]}],"code_released":[],"missing_for_reproduction":["Lens model and source-plane reconstruction code or parameters","Cell/image size and channel settings","Line-free channel ranges","Band 9 manual calibration script","Uncertainty propagation to n_e"],"estimated_data_volume_inferred":"~50-150 GB raw for Bands 8 and 9 (a few execution blocks)","score_inferred":3,"score_reason":"Data and main formulas are clear, but the lens model and several imaging settings are external or unstated.","rediscovery_candidate":false,"rediscovery_reason":"Depends on the lens model and source-plane reconstruction from another paper, and the recipe lacks several imaging details.","methods_papers":[{"citation":"(cite: warren_semilinear_2003)","why":"Semi-linear inversion lens reconstruction method"},{"citation":"(cite: goldsmith_herschel_2015)","why":"N+ rate equation formalism"},{"citation":"(cite: tayal_electron_2011)","why":"N+ electron collision rates"}],"companion_papers":[{"citation":"(cite: geach_magnified_2018)","why":"Band 4 CO(4-3) and CI(1-0) data and the lens model"},{"citation":"(cite: harrington_red_2019)","why":"Earlier [N II] 205 um SFR comparison assuming low n_e"}],"related_projects_or_surveys":["Spacewarps","Planck","Herschel","Atacama Cosmology Telescope"]}
